// Six equal bars. 5:3 is the common proportion; the designer's image is 541 by 330.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Aroamory flag"
  designer "NonMonoPrideFlags (DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2016-07-07"
  source "https://www.deviantart.com/nonmonoprideflags/art/Aroamory-Pride-Flag-620278659"
  note "Designer's own DeviantArt post, 'Aroamory Pride Flag', read live: 'This is my design for a Aroamory Pride Flag', with aroamory defined as a lack of romantic attraction while also not desiring any sort of romantic relationship. DeviantArt's page dates it 2016-07-07. The post gives no meanings, hex values or proportion."
  note "The colors were read from the post's image (541 by 330 pixels as DeviantArt serves it, taken as PNG; the bar edges show JPEG ringing, so values were read mid-bar): red #ed1b24, green #3da542, light green #a8d379, white #ffffff, grey #a9a9a9, black #000000, in six equal bars of 55 pixels. Below the red, these are the aromantic flag's bars."
  note "The image's 541:330 is not a usual flag proportion and doesn't look deliberate, so the common 5:3 is used here."
}
palette {
  red "#ed1b24"
  green "#3da542"
  light-green "#a8d379"
  white "#ffffff"
  grey "#a9a9a9"
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars red green light-green white grey black
